  "kernel": "79967860d4f6dc5e315502756ef88a2f04cf4004",
  "kernel_repo": "Aiden-HQ/AidenHQ",
  "notes": [
    "May add authority (grants, writes, roles or secrets) in: agent-builder, ai-reviewer. Auto-updates accept it; turn them off to review first.",
    "The kernel drives every record's review, started by the switch",
    "A rejected request comes back only after a fix",
    "The kernel plans kernel.apply, and a module with role kernel.apply files it",
    "The kernel brokers the GitHub code host's operations, under an owner-approved grant",
    "Check jobs run in credential-free launcher boxes on code host snapshots",
    "A job's next-turn requests reach its task's next admission",
    "Release names take a fourth part for a day's second cut",
    "Installs from a release update themselves overnight",
    "Kernel.apply runs in the kernel and never starts an apply twice",
    "Following a release is the owner's tap: release pins and auto-updates back on",
    "A closed task's workspace goes after three days",
    "A module files a task for the agent holding a role, once per source",
    "Stale routine runs are closed by the kernel",
    "Recurring runs start from the board",
    "A module with role kernel.owner-notice queues an owner message",
    "The code host service gets its mounts, its token and the kernel's workspace binding",
    "A routine run's wake names its routine, so the routine's own model applies",
    "In-box aidenhq commands file kernel writes with the job token",
    "A dispatcher finds its own job by the wake it admitted on"
  ],
  "release": "2026.11.18"
}
